WEBVTT

00:14:28.871 --> 00:14:31.662
and spend more time thinking
like a scientist,

00:14:31.662 --> 00:14:33.912
which is something I think we could
all learn to do better.

00:14:34.871 --> 00:14:37.121
It's funny, in the book,
you say how I think

00:14:37.121 --> 00:14:38.579
the first time you were called
The Logic Bully,

00:14:38.579 --> 00:14:41.829
it actually was something that you liked,
that at first it appealed to you.

00:14:42.496 --> 00:14:46.454
I was proud. I thought, yeah, that's
my job as a social scientist.

00:14:46.454 --> 00:14:52.121
I want to decimate your bad arguments with
rigorous evidence and airtight logic.

00:14:52.121 --> 00:14:53.537
And I'm good. And then, yeah,

00:14:53.746 --> 00:14:56.162
I didn't like the bully part so much
as I thought about it more.

00:14:56.662 --> 00:15:00.246
Given that, what are some of
your favorite practices